+`TCP_DEFER_ACCEPT` alone cost 6% in that regime. One side finding is worth keeping: `TCP_NODELAY` is
+inherited from the listener (kept). An earlier version of this section claimed that `read_nonblock`
+on a Ruby socket allocates a 4 KB IO buffer that lives as long as the connection; on Ruby 4.0.7 it
+does not. With an explicit output String, `ObjectSpace.memsize_of(socket)` stays 288 bytes before
+and after the read, and memory per connection stays at 3–5 KB with `read_nonblock`.
 
